<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 22 July, from 1209 to 1933.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1209</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Crusaders sack Béziers and massacre its people</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The army of the Albigensian Crusade stormed Béziers and killed much of its population. A chronicler later attributed to the papal legate the words 'Kill them all; God will know his own'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1298</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward I defeats William Wallace at Falkirk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">English longbowmen broke the Scottish spear formations at Falkirk, ending Wallace's career as a field commander. He was captured and executed in 1305.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1587</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John White's colonists arrive at Roanoke Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">More than 100 English settlers led by John White landed at Roanoke, intending to found the 'City of Ralegh'. When White returned in 1590 they had vanished, becoming the 'Lost Colony'.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1864</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hood attacks Sherman in the Battle of Atlanta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate General John Bell Hood struck Sherman's armies east of Atlanta, killing Union General James McPherson. The attack failed, and Atlanta's fall in September boosted Lincoln's re-election.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1933</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wiley Post completes the first solo flight around the world</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wiley Post landed at Floyd Bennett Field, New York, after circling the globe alone in 7 days, 18 hours and 49 minutes. An autopilot and radio direction-finder made the feat possible.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></li></ol>
